and partners  using api programs ticketmaster for  example  is today selling tickets not only  through their own portal  but also they have they are leveraging  their partners using  apis to sell their tickets and improve  the overall fan  experience and digital companies  for example accuweather who has been a  customer of apigee for a long period of  time  has actually opened up a new revenue  stream using apis  today they are exposing uh key weather  data  through apis to external developers not  only through a developer portal  but also through third-party  marketplaces and  they are also making those apis  available for businesses to embed them  into their business applications and all  this is happening  through api programs and this has helped  them  unlock new revenue streams and open up  new markets  so as apis are powering innovation  across these  segments what does this mean for  operations teams  as you continue to power your business  critical applications  and services with apis there is an  increasing pressure on operations teams  to stay on top of them especially from a  security perspective  so some of the challenges that they face  today are  to gain complete visibility into the  security attributes of the apis  to ensure that whatever developers are  building  are compliant with the industry and  organizations compliance requirements  they also want to make sure that  whenever there is an  incident they want to know about that  incident even if it  impacts their business and if at all  there is an incident  and that is impacting they want to be  able to very quickly diagnose and  identify the root cause  of the issue so that they can take the  most  appropriate remedial actions and resolve  the issues  faster as far as as possible on the  other hand what is also happening  is as you build and scale your api  programs  there is the goldmine of api data that  is being collected on the backend  right and api management platforms like  apigee  have a great opportunity to leverage  this data  to actually help customers one  improve the availability and performance  of the apis  and number two to also ensure that the  apis are secure  and meet the compliance requirements so  across the entire value chain  all the way from your target back-end to  front-end consumers  there is this large amount of metadata  that rpg  is also collecting at the back-end so if  you look at the apigee api management  platform today  it is google cloud's comprehensive full  lifecycle aka management platform  which includes a runtime layer a  mediation engine  api analytics and also provides you a  developer portal  and monetization capability but the way  we are leveraging the api data today  is by providing three different kind of  metrics for three different personas for  somebody like a product manager  we provide developer engagement metrics  and for a business persona we are  looking at business metrics such as  revenue generation etc  and for an operations persona today we  have  a deep deeply integrated monitoring  capability  what we are introducing today is api  security reporting which is  a new added functionality which is also  leveraging the same api data  what we have seen in most of our  customers is that depending on the size  of the customer because depending on the  nature of their business  they have either an ops person looking  into the security attributes or there is  a set of  person dedicatedly looking at the  security attributes  so this feature essentially targets both  the  current i.t admin or or ops persona  and also the setups persona so let's  learn a little bit about this new  feature that we just had what is api  security reporting  it provides deep insights for operations  teams  to basically do three very important  things  one is to ensure that all the apis that  are being developed by the development  teams  are adhering to the security and  compliance requirements  number two is to ensure that the  sensitive data within the organization  is  not abused by internal or external users  and number three is when there is an  incident it provides you  the capabilities to quickly identify  and diagnose the root cause and quickly  take familial actions to solve it  let's get into each of these  functionalities in detail security  compliance  is essentially a functionality that  addresses  the design time governance of the  product  it is about ensuring that developers who  are the core power users of our platform  are building apis that incorporate all  the policies  required by the compliance team in many  cases  we have seen customers who think that  you know the  the apis that are being built are by  default  adhering to all the policies but only  when something breaks  they actually realize that that's not  the that's not the real that's not  really happening  on the field right and with this feature  users can quickly identify proxies  that do not that do not adhere to  traffic security  and extension policy requirements and  users will also be able to very quickly  review  what are the shade flow configurations  and revisions for each of those proxies  and you can also analyze which host  which virtual host and ports are open to  receiving  secure traffic as compared to unsecured  traffic  as we discussed earlier several  enterprises  are today powering business critical  applications  to apis so there is a lot of sensitive  data that gets actually  involved in this api for example  developer information  trace sessions api keys all of these are  attributes that are vulnerable for  vulnerable to abuse from internal and  external users  so with this new feature users can  very closely monitor who within your  organization  is actually accessing the sensitive  information  and if there are any anomalies in that  access pattern you can you can discover  or  detect those suspicious behavior apigee  by default provides or also provides  ways for you to extract information  outside of the platform through  management apis  and it becomes extremely critical for  the operations teams  to make sure to monitor those users who  are  actually extracting this data out of the  platform  so on top of all the logging  capabilities that  apigee offers today data protection  is one one additional feature that helps  you to  look at all the user activity that is  happening  inside your off and the third capability  that we brought up is  precision diagnosis physician diagnosis  essentially addresses the runtime  governance piece of the security  it gives users insights into  what percentage of traffic is secured  versus non-secure  and when there is an security incident  you can quickly analyze which apps are  causing causing those security incidents  and which back-end targets are actually  getting affected  because of that you can also identify  anomalies in traffic patterns identify  the root causes for those anomalies  and basically take the most appropriate  remedial actions to solve this  what is happening with this capability  is that a lot of  operations teams find it very useful in  terms of  overall reducing their overall mean time  to diagnose  an issue and also the mean time to take  remedial actions  so with that let's just take a quick  break from the slide  and actually go into the product and  take a quick demo of this  so this is the apigee api console and  if you go to the analyze section on the  left  menu just below the api monitoring which  we launched last year there  is api security reporting this is the  new feature  go to the overview page so uh there is a  functionality for users to actually  look at this from four different  timelines you can look at the last one  hour  last one day seven days and even thirty  days so let's look at the last seven  days data  so what you see at the first glance is  the northbound traffic  this is the traffic that is coming into  the rpg api platform  and you can see across different  environments  what are the number of proxies that are  deployed  what you see here as active proxies are  the  are the proxies that are actually  receiving traffic  and 16 is essentially the number of  processes that have been deployed  and against each of these environments  you can see  the amount of traffic that is coming in  and what is the percentage  change so if you kind of uh  predict that you know this kind of  change that you see  in this environment is something very  alarming  or it is it is uncommon then you can  quickly  look at the runtime reports and see  what's actually happening there  we will see that just in about a minute  you will also see the traffic  per region this is especially useful  for customers who have proxies deployed  across several regions  and when there is traffic coming from  the various  regions and when there is an security  incident  it will be very easy for the ops person  to look at the abnormalities  in a specific region and quickly drill  down into that region and see what  exactly  is happening okay and if you  have logged into this uh platform as an  org admin  what you will also see is user activity  and by the way this feature is available  only for the org admins you can quickly  see  who are the users that are accessing the  platform and this is for the time window  that we selected here which is seven  days  you will see the number of ui ui  pings and you will see the number of api  usage  and also see the change in the activity  and what is the sensitive operations  that they are accessed  let's learn a little bit about user  activity  so again i come to user activity i'm  selecting the last seven days data  so what you see here is list of all the  users  within this particular arc which is  selected who  have been accessing the arc for the last  seven days  and you can see at the number of logins  number of  ui operations and apis is essentially  the management apis  that have been accessed by users over  this period of time  and when there is a change in activity  you can see the abnormalities here  and this is where exactly you will see  the sensitive operations of the user  so what is sensitive operations the way  we have defined sensitive operations  is when a user is accessing information  that contains either developer  information  app information virtual host trace  sessions  or customer or custom reports and  let's say if there is one particular  user who has  who has accessed a lot of sensitive data  and if you feel that  this user is not supposed to be  accessing that  you can very quickly you know contact  that user and take the most  appropriate action  what we also have here is the compliance  page  this is the design time governance  aspect that i was talking about earlier  so here the first thing that you can do  is  look at the various environments and  select the right environment that you  want to look in  and then you will see the list of all  the proxies  as well as their relevant revision  number  against that and what you also see here  is the number of policies that have been  configured for each of these proxies  these policies include traffic policy  security policy as well as extension  policy  what you will also see is the number of  shade flows that are configured for each  of the proxies  and you will also be able to see whether  this particular proxy  has been receiving secure traffic https  versus unsecured traffic on non-https  and let's click on one of these and see  what additional information you can see  here so when you click on this  on the right hand panel you will also  see the details of the policies that  have con  that have been configured against these  policies  and on the shared flows you will  basically see  the list of all the shared flows that  have been configured  and when you select a shared flow you  will also see  the policies that are configured against  this particular  shared flow and what we also have  here is the target view  target view essentially will give you  information  about that particular whether the  receive secure traffic  versus non-secure traffic in several  cases  we have also seen that you know  customers have  realized that some of the targets have  been configured to receive  non-https traffic and after using this  feature in alpha they kind of very  quickly  were able to change the configurations  to ensure that  it receives only the secure traffic  and the third component that i want to  talk about  is runtime this is the runtime  governance aspect  and just like compliance you can also  select  you know the environment that you want  to look at  you can change the timeline here  and you can also select regions if you  have multi-regions  and look at the traffic that is flowing  into  each of these proxies so what you see  here is the traffic  over the selected period of time and the  percentage change  and what percentage is http request  versus non-https  you will also be able to quickly see  what are the apps that  are accessing this proxy and if there is  any abnormality  so let's take a situation and understand  this a little better  if there is a high percentage change  in the traffic that is coming to a  particular proxy  and i see i as an ops person i are as a  cops person  i understand that this is something that  is not supposed to happen  and that is coming mostly from a  non-secure  force then i will be very quickly able  to  understand which app is causing that  traffic  and once i know that i will be able to  take the most familiar actions  and to them to mitigate the damage that  is happening i can also look at  which target is actually being affected  because of that abnormality so this  kind of you know significantly reduces  the overall time to understand what is  going wrong  with that particular proxy and take the  most in the action  so that is that is all about the new  security reporting feature  that we launched if you have any further  questions please feel free to reach out  to us  and if you are not an apigee edge  customer please do download the free  trial and start using this  thank you so much for joining us and  have a nice rest  you

